{"questions":[{"question_id":"9bcTVagaPVKeNtq6","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 2 Offline","year":2010,"examDate":2010,"subject":"physics","chapter":"properties-of-matter","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"surface-tension-excess-pressure-and-capillarity","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":0.75,"permalink":"when-liquid-medicine-of-density-rho-is-to-be-put-in-th-2010-marks-3-9bctvagapvkentq6.htm","content":"When liquid medicine of density <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.17ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 517 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is to be put in the eye, it is done with the help of a dropper. As the bulb on the\ntop of the dropper is pressed, a drop forms at the opening of the dropper. We wish to estimate the size of the drop.\nWe first assume that the drop formed at the opening is spherical because that requires a minimum increase in its\nsurface energy. To determine the size, we calculate the net vertical force due to the surface tension T when the\nradius of the drop is R. When the force becomes smaller than the weight of the drop, the drop gets detached from the\ndropper.\n<p>After the drop detaches, its surface energy is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"1.4 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\